/Temp/claim-check-0033-summary.txt\\\"\", \"description\": \"Remove the temp summary file\"}\nClaim-check of spec 0033 is complete: **40 assumption-shape claims audited — 39 CONFIRMED, 1 REFUTED-COUNT-STALE.** The report is at `specs/0033/.claim-check-json` and a decision entry was appended to `.history` via the safe writer.\n\n**Process:** The `.spec-md` on disk hashed to the expected canonical SHA (`ed4f3a12…`) via the spec-writer's helper, so the audit ran against the cycle's view of the spec. Every claim matching the assumption-shape phrase set (`existing`, `already`, `today`, `unchanged`, `stay`/`kept`, `currently unused`, plus inferred \"moved from\"/\"is removed\"/\"the missing X\" phrasings, noted as inferred in their evidence) was extracted, classified, and resolved against the repo with Read/Grep/Glob.\n\n**The one refuted claim** (id 10, §A.0): *\"the only proxy is the read-only picker `LibraryProxy` (`ElementId.fs:179`)\"*. The pointer itself is good — `LibraryProxy` exists at that line and is indeed read-only — but the quantifier \"only\" is stale: `ExperimentProxy` also exists in the same Domain file at `ElementId.fs:665`. Cheap operator fix: qualify it (e.g. \"the only *catalogue* proxy\") or drop \"only\".\n\n**Notable confirmations among the 39:**\n- All engine pointers land exactly: `…WithDisp` types (Dispersion.fs:9/24/38/53), `…Value` types and constructors (MaterialProperties.fs:50/101/127/76/87/112/139/187), `Rotation` spine (Geometry.fs:578/601/604/616/622), `Layer.rotate` (Media.fs:30).\n- The §A.0 problem statement is accurate: `sampleToSystem` string-branches on the four sample ids at Propagation.fs:139-141/157/172/180, and `propertiesOf` falls back to transparent glass at :104-111.\n- Negative existence claims verified: no 222/monoclinic/triclinic `Rho` builders in Active.fs (0 grep hits), and `plot.Axes.Right` has zero production-code uses (hits only in spec prose).\n- The Part D/E wiring claims hold precisely: chart style spine (ExperimentChart.fs:152/199/229/261/281, ChartWindow.fs:133/151/178), ScottPlot.Avalonia 5.1.59 in both fsprojs (:75, :173), and TestWindows referencing only Domain (:79) and Controls (:81).\n- One minor note recorded inside confirmed claim 22: the existing `LibraryControls.UiIds` bindings are plain `let` strings, not `[<Literal>]`-annotated — the spec's `[<Literal>]` wording reads as a prescription for the new modules rather than a property of the existing file.\n\nNo Markdown summary or counts were placed in the report file itself (claims array only, per the Phase 4 contract); `.spec-md` and the production tree were not touched.\nClaim-check of spec 0033 is complete: **40 assumption-shape claims audited — 39 CONFIRMED, 1 REFUTED-COUNT-STALE.** The report is at `specs/0033/.claim-check-json` and a decision entry was appended to `.history` via the safe writer.\n\n**Process:** The `.spec-md` on disk hashed to the expected canonical SHA (`ed4f3a12…`) via the spec-writer's helper, so the audit ran against the cycle's view of the spec. Every claim matching the assumption-shape phrase set (`existing`, `already`, `today`, `unchanged`, `stay`/`kept`, `currently unused`, plus inferred \"moved from\"/\"is removed\"/\"the missing X\" phrasings, noted as inferred in their evidence) was extracted, classified, and resolved against the repo with Read/Grep/Glob.\n\n**The one refuted claim** (id 10, §A.0): *\"the only proxy is the read-only picker `LibraryProxy` (`ElementId.fs:179`)\"*. The pointer itself is good — `LibraryProxy` exists at that line and is indeed read-only — but the quantifier \"only\" is stale: `ExperimentProxy` also exists in the same Domain file at `ElementId.fs:665`. Cheap operator fix: qualify it (e.g. \"the only *catalogue* proxy\") or drop \"only\".\n\n**Notable confirmations among the 39:**\n- All engine pointers land exactly: `…WithDisp` types (Dispersion.fs:9/24/38/53), `…Value` types and constructors (MaterialProperties.fs:50/101/127/76/87/112/139/187), `Rotation