.**\n\n**Decisions** — five `include` rows appended to `specs/0033/.gate-history` (using the pinned cycle timestamp `2026-07-05T23:43:10Z` and commit ref `4487b0b`), and `specs/0033/.spec-bundle` now carries `gates: [build, unit-tests, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, ui-tests]` — matching the operator's checked selection verbatim:\n\n- **build** — every part (A–G) edits F# sources across `Berreman/**`, so the whole-solution Release build applies universally.\n- **unit-tests** — Part B lands in the engine (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`) and `OpticalProperties/Active.fs` (the new 222/monoclinic/triclinic `Rho` builders and `toRhoWithDisp`), which `BerremanTests` covers.\n- **constructor-unit-tests** — Parts A (structural samples, Guid-backed ids, in-memory `MaterialProxy`/`SampleProxy`), the Domain side of B (`MaterialComplexity`, `DispersionModels` lowering), E (pure `SampleStackEditor`), F (window-free editor models) and G (RII formulas 2–7 in Storage) all land in projects `OpticalConstructor.Tests` references.\n- **ui-smoke / ui-tests** — Parts C–F add rendered surfaces (Materials/Library bays, the chart control real-moved into Controls with the second Y axis, both editor windows). I verified `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` references `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows` (line 124) and thereby Controls, so the headless smoke and per-panel suites genuinely reach the new views — the gates' `applies_to` globs list only Ui/App paths, but the test assemblies compile against everything the spec touches.\n\n**Why no `propose-new`** — every testable aspect of the spec maps onto an existing test project that an existing gate runs; proposing was the last-resort path and wasn't reached. No exclusions either: nothing in the spec removes a gated subsystem. All five gates are `filter: none`, so no `select` lists were emitted.\n\n**Bookkeeping** — one `gates`/`agent`/`decision` row was appended to `.history` via the `history_cli` safe writer (14 rows total now); the temp payload file was removed. Line-ending hygiene checked: `.gate-history` is pure LF, and I converted the CRLF my `.spec-bundle` edit introduced back to LF (`git diff --numstat` shows exactly the 7-insertion/1-deletion gates-array change). `.history`'s working-copy CRLF comes from the safe-writer CLI itself, as in prior cycles, and git normalizes it to LF on commit.\n\nUnrelated note: the session reported that the claude.ai Gmail / Google Calendar / Google Drive connectors need re-authorization via your claude.ai connector settings before they can be used; this run didn't need them.\nThe gates cycle for spec 0033 is complete: **all five existing gates are included, and no new gate needed to be proposed.**\n\n**Decisions** — five `include` rows appended to `specs/0033/.gate-history` (using the pinned cycle timestamp `2026-07-05T23:43:10Z` and commit ref `4487b0b`), and `specs/0033/.spec-bundle` now carries `gates: [build, unit-tests, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, ui-tests]` — matching the operator's checked selection verbatim:\n\n- **build** — every part (A–G) edits F# sources across `Berreman/**`, so the whole-solution Release build applies universally.\n- **unit-tests** — Part B lands in the engine (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`) and `OpticalProperties/Active.fs` (the new 222/monoclinic/triclinic `Rho` builders and `toRhoWithDisp`), which `BerremanTests` covers.\n- **constructor-unit-tests** — Parts A (structural samples, Guid-backed ids, in-memory `MaterialProxy`/`SampleProxy`), the Domain side of B (`MaterialComplexity`, `DispersionModels` lowering), E (pure `SampleStackEditor`), F (window-free editor models) and G (RII formulas 2–7 in Storage) all land in projects `OpticalConstructor.Tests` references.\n- **ui-smoke / ui-tests** — Parts C–F add rendered surfaces (Materials/Library bays, the chart control real-moved into Controls with the second Y axis, both editor windows). I verified `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` references `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows` (line 124) and thereby Controls, so the headless smoke and per-panel suites genuinely reach the new views — the gates' `applies_to` globs list only Ui/App paths, but the test assemblies compile against everything the spec touches.\n\n**Why no `propose-new`** — every testable aspect of the spec maps onto an existing test project that an existing gate runs; proposing was the last-resort path and wasn't reached. No exclusions either: nothing in the spec removes a gated subsystem. All five gates are `filter: none`, so no `select` lists were emitted.\n\n**Bookkeeping** — one `gates`/`agent`/`decision` row was appended to `.history` via the `history_cli` safe writer (14 rows total now); the temp payload file was removed. Line-ending hygiene checked: `.gate-history` is pure LF, and I converted the CRLF my `.spec-bundle` edit introduced back to LF (`git diff --numstat` shows exactly the 7-insertion/1-deletion gates-array change). `.history`'s working-copy CRLF comes from the safe-writer CLI itself, as in prior cycles, and git normalizes it to LF on commit.\n\nUnrelated note: the session reported that the claude.ai Gmail / Google Calendar / Google Drive connectors need re-authorization via your claude.ai connector settings before they can be used; this run didn't need them."}
